  "passage": "The city published open data about bus times, parks, public toilets, and air quality. Anyone could use the information to build apps or study problems.\nA student group used the data to make a map of bus stops without shade. They found that many were in neighborhoods with more older residents.\nTheir report helped the city decide where to add shelters first.\nOpen data sounded boring at first. Then students saw that it could support fairness.\nInformation locked away helps only a few people. Information shared responsibly can help communities ask better questions and demand better answers.",
